{{Short description|Conurbation in the Alpujarra of Balisca}}

'''Concordia''' ({{Literal translation|harmony|concord}}; {{Langx|kp|Apúchína|4=gathering place}}), also known as the '''Alpujarra Megalopolis''' (Baliscano: ''Megalopoli de Alpujarra'') or simply '''Alpujarras''', is a [[w:conurbation|conurbation]] and [[Megaregions of Balisca|megaregion]] in the [[Baliscan Confederation]]. Centered on the [[Salto Bay]] in South-central of the island of [[Atlántida]] it runs primarily northwest to southeast from the northern outskirts of [[León]] in [[Tukupi]], to the southern suburbs of [[Carabassa]] ([[Vitacura]]) and the northern outskirts of [[Syracuse]] ([[Piedmont]]).

Home to approximately 36 million people (representing around 26% of Balisca's total population), Concordia contains many urbanized [[communes of Balisca|communes]] with nationally significant landmarks and {{W|protected area}}s, along with renowned regional parks and indigenous communities, all connected by a [[Transport in Concordia|complex multimodal transportation network]]. The conurbation is known for its natural beauty, progressive politics, world-class universities, technology companies, and [[W:Social progress|social development]]. It encompasses the major cities of [[Castejón]], [[Valparaíso]] and [[Jatiel]], along with their metropolitan areas and smaller {{W|satellite cities}} (i.e. [[Yerba Buena]], [[León]], [[Amposta]], [[Syracuse]] and [[Carabassa]]). 

As of 1 January 2024, the conurbation had an estimated GDP of $2.021 trillion when calculated in terms of [[w:Purchasing power parity|purchasing power parity]], translating to a $55,815 GDP per capita. It is one of the [[W:List of cities by GDP|world's most productive metropolitan regions]], and represents 31.7% of Balisca's total [[W:Gross domestic product|gross domestic product]]. As a center of many industries, including [[W:Alternative finance|alternative finance]], fintech, [[W:International trade|international trade]], news and traditional media, [[W:Construction industry|construction]], education, fashion, [[W:Entertainment industry|entertainment]], tourism, [[W:Biotechnology|biotechnology]], law, and [[W:Robotics|robotics]], the Concordia region is one of the most prominent economic regions in the world. It also has a rich ecosystem of [[W:startup company|startups]], incubators, and accelerators in the fields of [[W:Agile software development|agile tech]], {{W|biotech}}, medical tech, and [[W:Social innovation|social innovation]]. 

The communes of Concordia rank among the overall best region in metrics such as healthcare, [[W:E-democracy|e-democracy]], access to education, and [[Transport in Balisca#Modal share|modal share]]. If considered a single region, Concordia has the highest regional median average income in Balisca, while simultaneously having the highest [[W:Income inequality|income inequality]]. A 2021 [[Instituto Confederal de Stadística]] (ICS) confederation-wide survey found Concordia overall to be the one of the "best areas to live in the future" based on 13 forward-looking measurements including [[Social Development Index|various economic, lifestyle, and health-related outlook metrics]].

